# How-to

Goal-oriented recipes. Each how-to answers one question: "how do I do X with
Wyrd?" Skip the explanation; go straight to the code.

## Build on Skald

- [Build an Agent](/how-to/build-an-agent/) — a bounded loop over a Prompt with tools, callbacks, and session memory.
- [Build a Workflow](/how-to/build-a-workflow/) — a DAG of Agent invocations, authored in Python, YAML, or Rust.

## Capability domains

- [Declare](/how-to/declare/) — author and register cards.
- [Evaluate](/how-to/evaluate/) — score agent runs and models against eval definitions.
- [Observe](/how-to/observe/) — read metrics, drift, and audit trails from a running system.
- [Operate](/how-to/operate/) — run, restart, and manage card-governed components.
- [Administer the gateway](/how-to/administer-the-gateway/) — provider credentials, deployments, and gateway policies.

<Aside title="What ships today" data-variant="wyrd">

Agent and Workflow recipes run on the Skald runtime today. Declare recipes are
available for the three shipped card kinds: Prompt, Model, and Data. Evaluate,
Observe, and Operate recipes follow as those capability contracts ship.

</Aside>
